<title>UK: EU sells free-mkt grains, rejects German intvn rye.</title>
<headline>EU sells free-mkt grains, rejects German intvn rye.</headline>
<text>
<p>LONDON, April 10 (Reuter) The European Union on Thursday</p>
<p>granted the following licences to export free market grain to</p>
<p>non-EU countries, member-country officials said.</p>
<p>		  Tonnage	  Maximum rebate</p>
<p>Soft wheat    172,300	   6.49  ecu/tonne</p>
<p>Barley	  296,000	  29.97  ecu/tonne</p>
<p>Bids for oats for export to Switzerland and Liechtenstein were rejected.</p>
<p>The EU rejected all bids in the weekly export tender to export German intervention rye to non-EU countries, the officials said.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
